     Dragon Saber-S ascended today with a personal best
(worst?) of 754562 points in 69755 turns.  Haven't seen many
posts about low scoreing ascensions, so I was wondering how
this did.  Game highlights and spoilers ...
^L













      As this was only my third ascension ever, I went for the
challenge of a low score rather than high.  Of course, all
standard rules applied, no backed up save game files, no
polypiling, cursed Bell tricks, Elbereth, or anything like
that.  Just a simple run away from the monsters and hide behind
your Archon style seemed to suffice.  
     Had a possible 16 wishes in this game, (2 from fountains,
1 from blessed magic lamp and 11 from recharged wands of
wishing plus 2 for the "zero" charge) and used 11 of them.  The
basic strategy says that to gain as few experience points as
possible let your pets do the fighting.  No gold or gems either.
      My first wish I got lucky dipping in a fountain and used it
on a nice Archon who evantually maxed out(Level 28, HP 224, AC -8).
Stayed with me until he got petrified by Medusa.  By then I had picked
up the ToM, and another WoW(3).  Only got up to level 11
experience wise and wasted a couple wishes to get potions of
gain level to go on the quest.  Went through two more "max
power" Archons before the game was through; one getting eaten
by a trapper, the other getting killed by a jabberwock.
Killing the Wiz on the way up was unavoidable, but I survived
although I lost the Amulet twice (only had a +3 Excalibur and
needed one hand free for a SoR) to double trouble.  GRRRR!
Most of the other wishes went to standard issue gear, GDSM,
HoOA, RoC, AoMB and so on.
       A couple things I learned about playing for a low score
and notes about the game in general.

  1.  Having an Archon early on was a HUGE help.  These guys
take out anything up to the Medusa level: shopkeepers, Priests,
vault guards, you name it.  Plus when they die you have a named
weapon and a SoR.

  2.  Having a magic whistle, GDSM and a ring of levitation
almost guarantees that you can keep your pet with you and
summon it when you need it.  GDSM works against teleport traps
and the ring of levitation gets you over those fall 4 levels
trapdoors.  I lost several characters to my formerly tamed but
now hostile pet Archon.

  3.  Wishes made the game almost too easy.  It was challenging
to try and elude monsters throughout the game but after a while
it was just technique and I still had several wishes left over.

  4.  Needless to say, ALWAYS check the curse/blessed state of
items.  Figuring that a Ghost pile scroll of genocide was
cursed, I deleted all wraiths on dungeon level 8.

  5.  Watch what your pet attacks.  Had to waste a wish on a
pick-axe after I got embedded in a wall following a guard out
of a vault.  Of course, Amaterasu Omikami was NO help.

  6.  Probably could have lowered my score further if I didn't
have to kill of the WoY 10 times.  Main problem was an
ineffective weapon.  No magic marker yet or enchant weapon
scrolls handy, plus no disintegration resistance meant I had to use
the +3 Excalibur and my SoR to take out the Wiz.  He doubled on me
three times, but a properly enchanted Tsurugi could have taken
him down early.

  7.  Could not find Ft. Ludios and ended the game with +5 GDSM,
+3 thoroughly damaged CoP, +2 HoOA and no other armor enchanted.
Just didn't have the markers to go scroll writing crazy.

  8.  Always have that wish handy for emergencies.  This game
can kill you in the drop of a hat so it doesn't hurt to be
prepared.

